# Diagram notes — lifecycle

Diagrams (`.puml`, `.drawio`) use **notes** (⚠ hypothesis, ✅ confirmed, risk) for open observations.

## When resolving a note

1. **Fold the note’s content** into the owning diagram element (container, relation, etc.) and into applicable text docs (`ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/architecture-gaps-and-questions.md`, `docs/client-documentation/README.md`).
2. **Remove the note** once reflected in shapes and prose.
3. If resolution surfaces new questions, add a fresh **⚠** note on the diagram and log it in `docs/architecture-gaps-and-questions.md`.

## Principle

Notes are temporary; confirmed facts belong **inside** diagram elements and in narrative docs, not in stray callouts forever.
